      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Maintenance Worker Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Maintenance Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Maintenance Worker Department MNC Job Description Title: Maintenance Worker Tech Department: Facility Services Category: Non-Exempt Hourly Summary/Objective Maintenance Worker reports to Maintenance Supervisor and assists in the physical upkeep of the College. Essential Functions This Tech position will have a focus on vehicle maintenance and repair. Proper use of equipment and facilities when necessary. Understand and adhere to governmental regulatory programs and policies. These may include but are not limited to: National Electrical Code, Environmental Protection Agency ( EPA ), Uniform Building Code ( UBC ) and local government environmental agency policies. Understand and interpret technical documents and diagrams which include but are not limited to: equipment manuals, blueprints, schematics, Single Line Electrical Drawings, mechanical and electrical equipment schematics. Inspect equipment before use and report unsafe conditions. This position is responsible for the care, maintenance, and repairs of all properties. Event set up and take down. Moving furniture and other items. Utilizes proper PPE for given duties. Performs other duties as assigned. Assist other Facilities Service teams as needed. Competencies Ethical Conduct. Stress Management/Composure. Teamwork Orientation. Thoroughness. Supervisory Responsibility This position has no supervisory requirements. Work Environment Strenuous physical activity. Facilities workers are required to move around campus properties and work with equipment. Outside work is required during all types of weather conditions. Facilities workers must use proper protective clothing as needed. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required as job duties demand. On-call work is required. Travel No travel is expected for this position. Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Required Qualifications High School diploma or 4 Years experience in field of focus. Valid driver’s license and clean driving record. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. The employee is occasionally required to sit, climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl. The employee must frequently lift or move up to 50 pounds and occasionally lift or move up to 75 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and ability to adjust focus. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S114P Number of Vacancies 2 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/455 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
